    "findings": [
      "The shared upstream graph requests GGML_PREC_F32 for flash attention. Stock F16-input CPU attention still narrows Q and accumulates V in F16; the retained port honors F32 arithmetic while retaining F16 K/V storage.",
      "The attention-only port exactly matches independent stock F32 attention for all 57 scored token NLL values and first-token top-eight logits in these two corpora. This supports the tested attention arithmetic and indexing; it is not a whole-model precision proof.",
      "The full port also retains scalar transcendental and recurrent-convolution arithmetic policies. Their combination changes the model trajectory relative to stock arithmetic.",
      "Removing only explicit recurrent-convolution FMA does not remove the initial logit discrepancy, although it changes later token NLL. Restoring only the two stock RoPE trigonometric calls also does not restore full numerical agreement.",
      "The observed first full-port/stock mismatch on the short code prefill is after attention layer 2; the preceding layer 0 and 1 output fingerprints match."
    ],
    "host_llamafile_on_off_same_fixture_results_exactly_equal": true
  },
  "limitations": [
    "The owned code/Russian corpora contain 57 scored LFM3 tokens; larger corpora and task-quality benchmarks remain separate.",
    "Functional arithmetic and identifier replies demonstrate completed final text, not strict formatting reliability.",
    "No long-context LFM3 quality, exact recurrent-state snapshot, production prefix-cache, GPU, prolonged-session or thermal qualification follows.",
    "Performance measurements and APK delivery verification are outside this summary.",
    "Metadata planning and supplied-budget admission checks at 4K/8K/16K/32K do not certify real-model generation or peak-memory safety at those contexts."
  ],
